WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.529
Modern applications often mix traditional server sessions with token-based approaches.

2
00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:09.057
A server-rendered web application may use an opaque cookie-backed session.

3
00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:13.133
A single-page application may call APIs with access tokens.

4
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:18.115
A mobile application may rely on tokens stored in platform-managed storage.

5
00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:22.190
Backend services may exchange credentials through an identity provider.

6
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:35.323
The architecture changes the mechanics, but the security questions stay familiar: who is this request for, what is it allowed to do, and is the session state still valid?

7
00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:38.946
Access tokens and refresh tokens need different handling.

8
00:00:38.946 --> 00:00:44.834
Access tokens are commonly short-lived credentials used to call APIs or access resources.

9
00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:52.985
Refresh tokens can allow the client to obtain new access tokens over time, so they are especially sensitive.

10
00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:57.061
Their storage, rotation, revocation, and reuse detection policies matter.

11
00:00:57.061 --> 00:01:04.307
Developers should not assume that a token is safe just because it uses a common format.

12
00:01:04.307 --> 00:01:09.288
Issuer, audience, expiration, signature, scope, and relevant claims still need validation.

13
00:01:09.288 --> 00:01:14.270
Single-page applications, mobile applications, and APIs introduce storage and cross-origin considerations.

14
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:21.968
Browser-accessible storage may be convenient, but it can create exposure if the application has client-side script weaknesses.

15
00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:26.044
Native mobile storage should use platform protections where available.

16
00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:31.479
APIs should validate tokens server-side and enforce authorization on every sensitive operation.

17
00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:37.366
Modern session management is not about choosing cookies or tokens as a slogan.

18
00:01:37.366 --> 00:01:43.706
It is about matching the storage, lifetime, validation, and renewal model to the application?

19
00:01:43.706 --> 00:01:47.329
s threat profile.
